      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Input",
        "body": "A bridge renderer consumes a bridge node plus the resolved target artifact metadata: icon surface, label, target ref, resource kind, scope, explicit grants, and any local policy reduction.",
        "required": true,
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/input.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-renderer-contract-output",
      "type": "output",
      "label": "Output",
      "position": {
        "x": 580,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 360,
      "height": 240,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Output",
        "body": "A bridge renderer produces a compact authority surface that shows target identity, target clarity, grants, scope, diagnostics, and action buttons only for capabilities explicitly granted.",
        "reversible": true,
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/output.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-renderer-contract-rule",
      "type": "rule",
      "label": "Rule",
      "position": {
        "x": -20,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Rule",
        "body": "A bridge renderer is authority-first, not content-first. It should show icon, label, target ref, grant chips, and permitted actions. It should not behave like a browser card, a semantic-zoom surface, or a rich content preview.",
        "severity": "high",
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/rule.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-renderer-contract-guardrail",
      "type": "guardrail",
      "label": "Guardrail",
      "position": {
        "x": 580,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Guardrail",
        "body": "Do not imply authority from target existence alone. If a grant is absent, the renderer must omit the affordance rather than showing a disabled promise of capability.",
        "hardStop": true,
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/guardrail.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-renderer-contract-failure",
      "type": "failure-mode",
      "label": "Failure Mode",
      "position": {
        "x": 1180,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Failure Mode",
        "body": "A weak bridge renderer makes authority ambiguous: it looks like a port card, hides the target, shows actions without grants, or participates in browser-facing semantic zoom. That makes the focused graph less governable.",
        "response": "refuse",
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/failure-mode.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-renderer-contract-procedure",
      "type": "procedure",
      "label": "Procedure",
      "position": {
        "x": 1180,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Procedure",
        "body": "Resolve target identity first, then grants and scope, then render compact diagnostics and action buttons. Prefer the target icon view for identity, show the target ref second, then expose create or runtime actions only when the explicit bridge grants allow them.",
        "steps": [
          "Read the host port authority; default new ports to navigate.",
          "Read the target exposure: named views, bridgeability, runtime capability, and default root behavior.",
          "Validate semantic meaning, direction, semantic type, multiplicity, and wildcard policy.",
          "Compute effective authority as the minimum of host authority, target exposure, and local policy.",
          "Filter the result to the allowed boundary behavior or refuse if no safe behavior remains."
        ],
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/procedure.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-renderer-schema-examples",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "9. Examples",
      "position": {
        "x": 1780,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 320,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## Examples\n\n**Valid:**\n- host.navigate_port -> target.root\n- host.consume_view -> target.port_view\n\n**Invalid (must fail):**\n- bridge authority inferred from a rendered card\n- runtime behavior granted because a target view happens to exist\n- incompatible semantic types connected without an explicit wildcard policy"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-renderer-schema-migrations",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "10. Migration Notes",
      "position": {
        "x": 1780,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## Migration Notes\n\nDocument explicit, reversible evolution for:\n\n- authority ladder changes\n- semantic type renames\n- multiplicity changes\n- default root policy changes\n- boundary filtering behavior\n\nMigration notes must preserve portability and avoid silent authority escalation."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-renderer-schema-human-notes",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "12. Human Notes",
      "position": {
        "x": -1820,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 280,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## Human Notes\n\nUse this space for rationale, stewardship notes, and examples that help humans maintain the port API without weakening the normative boundary rules."
        }
      }
    },
